{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.25,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the contested SGD 6.00 Changi Terminal 1 no-show fee cannot be decided on this record and is going to a human reviewer. The fee is placed on hold (fare_breakdown shows payment_status PENDING, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) — it is neither collected nor refunded while review is pending. An escalation is not a win for either side; it is a refusal to guess.\n\nThe fact that decides this case is whether the driver completed the mandatory 480-second in-geofence dwell for an AIRPORT pickup, measured under POL-NS-01(c) from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix and not from the arrived tap. The only artifacts that carry that fact are both impaired for policy purposes:\n- EV-GPS-00210 (driver device, weight 0.25; CLOCK_SKEW, GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE, TRUNCATED_LOG, LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, PARTIAL_RECORD). It is impaired under POL-NS-08(a) on a 228-second device clock skew, and under POL-NS-08(b) on a 186-second sampling gap sitting exactly across the entry moment, only 9 fixes in the trip, fewer than six across the waiting window, and a missing rider_track.\n- EV-TRIP-00210 (platform telemetry, weight 0.40; CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT), impaired under POL-NS-08(a) because it disagrees with the trace on the termination time by more than 90 seconds.\n\nOn the trace read at face value the first qualifying fix is 23:42:21 and the cancellation 23:49:05, a 404-second dwell 76 seconds short of 480. Corrected by the 228-second skew the same fix maps to 23:38:33 server time, a 632-second dwell comfortably over. The 186-second gap conceals the one moment that would choose between the two, so neither reading is established on admissible evidence.\n\nTurning to the claims that survived to this stage. The rider's two shortfall arguments — the 255-second longest qualifying run, and the trip record's own wait_time_min of 6.9 (414 seconds) against 480 — are accepted as pointing the same way, but each rests on an artifact impaired under POL-NS-08(a)/(b); such a claim cannot alone carry a finding against the party it disfavours, and the two figures do not agree with each other or with the skew-corrected trace. The driver's points are answered too: the RIDER_NO_SHOW termination code and the absence of a boarding event are not contested, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming guard genuinely does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d of 2 against the threshold of 4, and a rate of 0.013 against 0.08), so SGD 4.80 of compensation would have followed had the fee been chargeable — but chargeability is exactly what is undecided. The rider is not exonerated under POL-NS-04 either, because its limb (c) is undecidable on a missing rider_track and an undecidable limb is neutral rather than satisfied.\n\nBecause the only evidence for the deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08 limbs (a) to (d), that clause caps the ruling at PARTIAL_REFUND and sends the case to POL-NS-09. POL-NS-09(b) is also engaged: two admissible artifacts contradict each other directly on arrival and dwell and no clause resolves the conflict — clock-skew matching is unsafe under POL-NS-05 read with POL-NS-08(a), and the traffic_advisory that would let POL-NS-06(i) sum separate in-geofence intervals is MISSING at weight 0.0. Confidence is capped by POL-GEN-02(2) at the weight of the carrier of the deciding fact, 0.25, below the 0.70 floor, so POL-NS-09(a) is engaged as well. No clause produces a referral here: POL-NS-05(ii) does not fire because qualifying in-geofence fixes do exist, and the POL-NS-07 packet instruction does not fire because the anti-farming check does not trip.\n\nThe open question the reviewer must settle: resolve the 228-second clock skew and reconstruct the geofence-entry moment inside the 186-second gap to fix the true in-geofence dwell. If it reaches 480 seconds, the SGD 6.00 fee stands and SGD 4.80 compensation is payable to the driver under POL-NS-07; if it falls short, the fee is refunded in full to the rider under POL-NS-06 with no compensation payable."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "POL-NS-01 limb (d) fails on its own timing conjunct as well. The limb requires the trip to be terminated 'at or after the moment the required dwell elapsed', and limb (c) fixes the start of that dwell at the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not at the arrived tap. The first qualifying in-geofence fix on the trace is 23:42:21 and the trip was cancelled at 23:49:05, 404 seconds later - the driver pulled the plug 76 seconds before the 480th second. A cancellation that precedes the elapse of the required dwell cannot satisfy a limb written to require the opposite.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00210 at weight_multiplier 0.25 but does not name its issue code(s): CLOCK_SKEW, GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE, TRUNCATED_LOG, LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, PARTIAL_RECORD"
    },
    {
      "claim": "No time can be added to that dwell. POL-NS-06 limb (i) permits separate in-geofence intervals to be summed only where a present and populated traffic_advisory of type KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT covers the pickup road. The advisory artifact for this trip, EV-ADVIS-00210-01, is MISSING - no payload, weight 0.0 - so limb (i) is unavailable, no advisory can extend the driver's clock, and the derived facts record no second in-geofence interval to add in any event. The absence of any advisory covering the Changi T1 arrival kerb is itself citable, and it works against this charge rather than rescuing it.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00210-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Limb (b) of POL-NS-01 is not made out either. It requires the gps_trace to place the driver inside the pickup geofence 'at or before' the arrived event, and the earliest qualifying in-geofence fix on the trace is 23:42:21, which post-dates the trip record's 23:42:10 marker; the trace jumps from 23:39:15 to 23:42:21, so the 186-second gap swallows the moment of entry and no fix sits at the marker at all. The only route to limb (b) is to repair the timestamps using the 228-second device clock skew, and POL-NS-08(a) treats a skew over 90 seconds as an unsafe match between the arrived event and a GPS fix. POL-NS-01 is conjunctive and the party seeking the fee must carry every limb, so an unprovable limb (b) is a broken limb (b).",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00210 at weight_multiplier 0.25 but does not name its issue code(s): CLOCK_SKEW, GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE, TRUNCATED_LOG, LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, PARTIAL_RECORD"
    },
    {
      "claim": "If the panel cannot close on a full refund because the two sources contradict each other, the case still cannot close as a charge against the rider. The trace is impaired under POL-NS-08(b) - a 186-second gap straddling entry, fewer than six fixes across the waiting window, and rider_track omitted - and under POL-NS-08(a) on the 228-second clock skew; the chat log is impaired under POL-NS-08(c), carrying 2 of the 4 messages the trip record records for the 23:42-23:49 window (weight 0.60, TRUNCATED_LOG). The deciding fact is therefore carried only by artifacts of weight 0.25 and 0.40, so under POL-GEN-02 rule (2) confidence cannot exceed 0.40, below the 0.70 floor, and POL-NS-09 limbs (a), (b) and (e) all engage. Escalation holds the fee rather than collecting it - EV-FARE-00210 shows payment_status PENDING and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 - so on that footing too the rider does not carry the disputed charge.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-TRIP-00210 at weight_multiplier 0.4 but does not name its issue code(s): CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Fare integrity is not in issue, and the charge as itemised is correct. Under the fee schedule's resolution rule the chargeable cancellation fee is the GREATER of the zone-class fee and the vehicle-tier fee: AIRPORT is SGD 6.00 and RYDE_X is SGD 4.00, and the greater is exactly the SGD 6.00 itemised in fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee. POL-NS-08(d) is therefore not engaged, and EV-FARE-00210 — COMPLETE at weight 1.0 — reconciles precisely with this trip's zone class and vehicle tier.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-TRIP-00210 at weight_multiplier 0.4 but does not name its issue code(s): CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The driver reached the pickup geofence. EV-GPS-00210's derived driver_track puts his nearest approach at 96.01 m from the pickup pin at Changi Terminal 1 — inside the 150 m arrival radius POL-NS-02 sets for the AIRPORT zone class — and the derived arrival block records 5 consecutive qualifying in-geofence fixes against the 3 consecutive in-radius fixes POL-NS-02 requires. I disclose that EV-GPS-00210 is IMPAIRED at weight 0.25 on CLOCK_SKEW, GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE, TRUNCATED_LOG, LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD; the proximity and fix-count findings survive the discount because clock skew and truncation displace timestamps, not measured distances between fixes and the pin.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-TRIP-00210 at weight_multiplier 0.4 but does not name its issue code(s): CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "POL-NS-01 limb (b) is satisfied, or at worst undecidable — it is not affirmatively failed. The record's arrived event is 23:42:10 and the first qualifying in-geofence fix is 23:42:21, an eleven-second offset. EV-GPS-00210's own admissibility report measures a device clock skew of 228 seconds, twenty times that offset, so eleven seconds cannot establish that the driver was outside the geofence when he marked arrival. Read with the skew correction the same fix maps to 23:38:33 server time, some three and a half minutes before the marker. I rely on derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec, which is precisely the field the skew contaminates, and I disclose that both artifacts are impaired: EV-TRIP-00210 at weight 0.4 on CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT and EV-GPS-00210 at weight 0.25 on the six codes set out above.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00210 at weight_multiplier 0.25 but does not name its issue code(s): CLOCK_SKEW, GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE, TRUNCATED_LOG, LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, PARTIAL_RECORD"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The rider's POL-NS-06 shortfall case cannot be run on this trace, so no shortfall is established. EV-GPS-00210 covers 22.8% of the active window, holds a 186-second sampling gap sitting directly across the moment of geofence entry (23:39:15 to 23:42:21), and stops at 23:46:36 — 149 seconds before the cancellation at 23:49:05, over the 120-second truncation tolerance. Any dwell figure read off it is a floor rather than a measurement, and POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-08(b) say expressly that fixes too sparse to carry the test are impairment, not proof of absence. The artifact is IMPAIRED at weight 0.25 on CLOCK_SKEW, GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE, TRUNCATED_LOG, LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-TRIP-00210 at weight_multiplier 0.4 but does not name its issue code(s): CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The trip record's own wait_time_min of 6.9 does not establish a shortfall either. That figure is arrived_at 23:42:10 to cancelled_at 23:49:05, and arrived_at is the very event the trace contradicts; the artifact is IMPAIRED at weight 0.4 on CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT for exactly that reason. I do not ask the bench to convert the driver's own 'more than eight minutes' into 480 seconds on his say-so — I ask only that a number resting on a contested timestamp be given no weight in either direction.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00210 at weight_multiplier 0.25 but does not name its issue code(s): CLOCK_SKEW, GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE, TRUNCATED_LOG, LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, PARTIAL_RECORD"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The rider cannot be exonerated under POL-NS-04, which requires all three of its limbs. Limb (a) needs a locating or coordinating message during the waiting window; the only rider message on the export is MSG-00210-004 at 23:49:40, thirty-five seconds after the driver terminated the trip at 23:49:05. Limb (c) cannot be satisfied at all: EV-GPS-00210 carries no rider_track, so the presence test is undecidable, and POL-NS-04's own text makes an undecidable limb (c) neutral — neutral is not satisfied, and a clause requiring all three limbs exonerates nobody on two. EV-CHAT-00210 is IMPAIRED at weight 0.6 on TRUNCATED_LOG, messages 002 and 003 being absent from the 23:42 to 23:49 window, so the export is not a complete picture; but it is the only chat evidence in the bundle, and on it limb (a) is not made out.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-TRIP-00210 at weight_multiplier 0.4 but does not name its issue code(s): CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "EV-TRIP-00210 and EV-GPS-00210 are two admissible artifacts that contradict each other directly on arrival and on dwell — 23:42:10 with a 6.9-minute wait on one side, a first qualifying in-geofence fix at 23:42:21 with a 255-second qualifying run and 22.8% coverage on the other — and no clause in this policy resolves which is right. The sole evidence for the deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08 limbs (a) and (b), which on that clause's own terms caps the ruling and sends the case to a reviewer under POL-NS-09. Escalation holds the SGD 6.00 fee on its present PENDING status rather than refunding it, which is the disposition the evidence actually supports.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-TRIP-00210 at weight_multiplier 0.4 but does not name its issue code(s): CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "No traffic advisory covers the Changi Terminal 1 arrival kerb in this window. EV-ADVIS-00210-01 is MISSING, keeps its identifier and carries weight 0.0, and the absence is itself citable. It means the record discloses no kerbside restriction, enforcement operation, closure or accident on the pickup road — nothing on the ground that would explain a driver unable to hold at the pin, and nothing that displaces the driver's account of waiting at Door 6.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00210-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
